From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:59:15 +0200
Subject: Suggest game-data-packager-runtime instead of recommending it

The runtime is the GTK launcher the generated game packages use (gdp-launcher) and Depends on
gir1.2-gtk-4.0 and friends: far too heavy for the 256 MB PS3, and Walnut does not use it. The
command line tool imports nothing from runtime/ (only the ScummVM and DOS packages it builds
reference the runtime, in their own dependencies). The runtime binary is still built.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -40,12 +40,12 @@ Depends:
 Recommends:
  7zip,
  cabextract,
- game-data-packager-runtime (>= ${source:Version}),
  innoextract,
  lhasa | jlha-utils | lzh-archiver,
  unshield,
  unzip,
 Suggests:
+ game-data-packager-runtime (>= ${source:Version}),
  arj,
  binutils,
  cdparanoia,
